  "supersedes": "Earlier capped-design release manifests and reports remain immutable historical evidence. They do not describe this candidate. Use the uncapped manifest linked here.",
  "policy": {
    "membership": "No numerical cap on pools or nonprofit ballot members. Onboarding and nonprofit configuration remain multisig/Timelock controlled.",
    "seed": "User-confirmed planning capacity is 300 seed-supported nonprofits; later onboarding is economically harder, not prohibited. No Seed, staking or reserve allocation contract was changed, and reserve economics were not independently re-audited in this task."
  },
  "implementation": {
    "preparation": "Safe start snapshots previous-block voters/stake and current fund allocations, fixes the pool-history boundary, opens the full 30-day Phase 1, and processes up to 100 IDs. Permissionless prepareBallot or executeCurrentCycle processes subsequent batches. Mapping-based deduplication preserves earliest admitted PID order. Phase 1 settlement requires preparation complete; the keeper advances it during Phase 1 and in the READY state. No extra Safe call is required.",
    "configurationTiming": "Pool IDs added after start are excluded. Removal status and charity wallet are read at processing time; approval is required when a recipient is first admitted. Already-admitted recipients cannot be rewritten or removed by later configuration changes. Staking has no historical nonprofit-configuration getter. An invalid batch reverts atomically; Timelock repair or pre-settlement cancellation is needed. This is distinct from the immutable voter/fund snapshot at Safe start.",
    "settlement": "Each nonprofit vote updates a constant-work running leader. Equal tallies favor the earlier ballot position even if votes arrive in reverse order. Settlement does not scan the ballot. Zero-vote rollover and Offering tie/zero-vote burn remain unchanged. Phase 2 starts with a full 30 days after actual Phase 1 settlement.",
    "compatibility": "Original storage slots and existing Cycle members remain in place; preparation fields, leader and position mapping are appended. Legacy maxBallotSize and its setter are retained for compatibility but ignored for membership. The advisory historical index is bounded per call and no longer used by cycle preparation. Active-cycle upgrade guards remain intact.",
    "events": "CycleStarted contains the initial batch for large cycles, not the complete ballot. Consumers must use BallotBatchPrepared/BallotPreparationCompleted or paginated getters. Each emitted batch is bounded.",
    "frontend": "Phase 2 ballot pages contain at most 100 entries each and are read at a single pinned block only after preparation is complete. Failed/incomplete reads fail rather than fabricate a ballot. Protocol Funds analytics display preparation progress. Existing selected-wallet signing protections are preserved.",
    "documents": [
      "README.md",
      "docs/THESIS.md section 5.5"
    ],
    "release": "Preflight no longer enforces the old numerical limits and reports preparation batch count. Keeper progresses Phase 1 batches automatically. New manifest created exclusively; old evidence was not rewritten."
  },
